## What was missing and what I did

The evaluator passed the code fix and failed one thing: the mandatory Docs step was skipped entirely. I fixed that, and found two more real problems on the way.

1. CLAUDE.md (the actual failure). Appended a Day-186 paragraph to the src/tools.rs bullet covering everything the task and evaluator required: the mechanism (benign_exit_note over the 10-entry BENIGN_EXITS table, emission point at StreamingBashTool::execute's exit_line, None = byte-identical), the exact-(command-word, exit-code) key and why grep 2 must stay unannotated, the pipeline/pipefail refusal, the COMMAND_WRAPPERS reuse-not-copy decision, the near-miss guards, the positive-control result, two stated limits, and the post count. Both evaluator greps now return non-zero.

2. I re-ran the positive control rather than quoting it from memory. Neutering benign_exit_note to always return None turned exactly one test red — benign_exit_note_fires_only_on_the_exact_command_and_code, receipt left: None, right: Some("no matches found") — while `benign_exit_note_refuses_pipelines_and_substitutions` stayed green. That's the direction that proves the near-miss guard tests the pass-through rather than the fix. Restore was byte-identical.

3. Unprompted finding: the previous commit was unformatted. Two assert_eq! lines were over width, so commit 5f1ee6a6 would have failed `cargo fmt -- --check` in CI. cargo fmt wrapped them (+6 lines), which then tripped the module-size gate at 3651 lines, 6 past its recorded 3645. I paid the register line with the number the gate itself printed rather than absorbing the drift — that's the Day-183 lesson in this very file, where 11 entries silently absorbed drift because nothing read the warnings. Gate is now silent.

