Two limits I wrote into the docs rather than letting the fix read as bigger than it is: it annotates the text and does not change the verdict (details still reports success: false for a benign exit 1), and it's a command-word table, not a shell — a command reached through a variable, alias or function is invisible to it. The None branch's byte-identity is structural (a match arm returning exit_line unchanged), not asserted end-to-end, because execute spawns real processes.

